[0, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2J\u001b[H\u001b[1;36m  zfsify  /  root backup and restore\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[38;5;245m  Ubuntu 24.04  ·  1 GiB RAM  ·  DigitalOcean  ·  60.99% used before conversion\u001b[0m\r\n  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;37m  01  A normal Ubuntu root, already more than half full\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  df -h /; du -h /srv/demo/archive.bin\r\n  \r\n  Filesystem      Size  Used Avail Use% Mounted on\r\n  /dev/vda1        24G   15G  9.1G  62% /\r\n  13G     /srv/demo/archive.bin\r\n  root@zfsify:~# curl -fsSL http://127.0.0.1:8765/reformat.sh | sh\r\n  \r\n  Root filesystem: /dev/vda1 on /dev/vda | used 60.99% (15177285632 / 24883167232 bytes)\u001b[31;1H\u001b[38;5;245m  Actual output · waits shortened · development build · full recording linked below\u001b[0m"]
[4, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2J\u001b[H\u001b[1;36m  zfsify  /  root backup and restore\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[38;5;245m  Ubuntu 24.04  ·  1 GiB RAM  ·  DigitalOcean  ·  60.99% used before conversion\u001b[0m\r\n  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;37m  02  Choose a full backup instead of discarding data\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\r\n  !! WARNING: ROOT IS AT LEAST 50% USED. PRESERVATION IS NOT ELIGIBLE.     !!\r\n  !! A: rclone backup, verify, reformat, then restore the full system.    !!\r\n  !! B: erase and install fresh Ubuntu with a limited priority restore.   !!\r\n  !! Applications and data are deleted. /etc, users, SSH keys and        !!\r\n  !! basic settings survive. There is no automatic fallback to erasure. !!\r\n  !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\r\n  Choose A for rclone backup/restore, or B (or y) for an ERASE install: A\u001b[31;1H\u001b[38;5;245m  Actual output · waits shortened · development build · full recording linked below\u001b[0m"]
